  "prefLabel": "Env-Sw 102.53 Depolymerization",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Sw 102.53 “Depolymerization” means “depolymerization” as defined in RSA 149-M:4, V-a, namely “a manufacturing process where post-use polymers are broken into smaller molecules such as monomers, oligomers, plastic or chemical feedstocks, or other basic raw materials.”\n\nSource. #14103, eff 10-23-24 (see Revision Note #2 at chapter heading for Env-Sw 100)",
